116
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:04,860
They told us they were ready to cancel the project.

117
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:06,860
Why?

118
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:14,560
Well, looking back, a big part of the reason was that the project had taken the safe route.

119
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:17,460
We'd focused primarily on technical success.

120
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,860
We'd been able to pull together a great team of smart people.

121
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:23,460
And the functionality we were demoing was really good.

122
00:06:23,460 --> 00:06:28,320
But it wasn't really what was most important to our organization.

123
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:33,360
What we had decided to do was migrate over one of our existing clients.

124
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:42,120
And that client was low risk, which made it easier for us, but also low value to the business.

125
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:47,860
So it didn't really matter much to them if we succeeded or not.

126
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:52,860
For example, we could import warranty data from our clients into our database.

127
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:56,060
But we hadn't delivered much more than basic functionality beyond that.

128
00:06:56,060 --> 00:07:01,360
And after giving a demo of our latest iterations work to them at the end of that year, this

129
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:03,960
