139
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:40,460
I was nervous about all the complicated business logic that we would be implementing later on.

140
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,760
It was lurking there, dangerous.

141
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:45,260
And one day it was going to surface.

142
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:47,260
You had that feeling on your projects sometimes?

143
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:50,860
Something had to change if we were to turn this around.

144
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:55,560
What could we do differently?

145
00:07:55,560 --> 00:08:00,960
Now what I've discovered in the last ten years is many so-called modernization or legacy

146
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:09,060
rewrite projects fall into the same trap that we did, you know, focusing on the things that

147
00:08:09,060 --> 00:08:14,160
